  "body": "## What changed\n\n`grblhal.cps`, `carvera.cps` and `tinyg.cps`: `xyFirst` now returns `false` when it refuses the first X/Y traverse because the stream states no ClearancePlane and no RetractPlane. Its callers write nothing for that move: `onRapid`, `onLinear`/`onCircular` (through `startXY`), and grblHAL's `onCycle`. X/Y stay unknown, so every later move of the section is refused the same way. The message is still given once per program. This is the rule the Tormach (#1614) and Fanuc-family (#1633) posts already follow.\n\nBefore this change, the refused rapid was still written as `G0 X20 Y10 Z2`, followed by the feeds. The app blocks the post on the warning, but the `post` CLI writes the file anyway, so the refused move ended up in the program text.\n\n**TinyG too.** The issue says TinyG already stops through `startXY`. Its `onRapid` still wrote the combined rapid after the refusal, though, and the issue's \"Done means\" pin covers TinyG, so TinyG's `onRapid` gets the same guard. The decision is recorded in `docs/decisions/1682-refused-traverse-writes-nothing.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/post/tests/first_traverse_clearance.rs`)\n\n- `a_first_traverse_with_no_stated_plane_is_refused_by_name`: now also asserts that no motion line carries an X or Y word, for grblHAL, TinyG and Carvera. It was red on the old scripts (grblHAL output: `G0 X20 Y10 Z2`, `G1 X20 Y10 Z-1 F500`, ...).\n- `no_xy_motion_follows_the_refusal_whatever_the_first_move` (new): the first move of the section is a feed, an arc or a canned cycle. For each case it checks that the refusal is given by name and that no X/Y word is written.\n\n**Mutation check.** I reverted each new guard line on its own, ran the suite, restored the file from a backup, touched it and compared it with `cmp`. Every mutation turned the suite red:\n\n| post | line mutated | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| grblhal / carvera / tinyg | `onRapid` guard dropped | 1 failed |\n| grblhal / carvera / tinyg | `xyFirst` refusal returns `true` | 2 failed |\n| grblhal / carvera / tinyg | `startXY` refusal check dropped | 2 failed |\n| grblhal / carvera | `onLinear` guard dropped | 2 failed |\n| grblhal / carvera | `onCircular` guard dropped | 1 failed |\n| grblhal | `onCycle` guard dropped | 1 failed |\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green. It ran 17 post suites (7 s) and 21 app suites, including `grblhal_post`, `carvera_post`, `tinyg_post` and `conformance` (97 s).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --test first_traverse_clearance -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- No golden G-code changed. Only streams that state no plane are affected, and those were already refused.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The batch gate was not run, to keep within the budget.\n- The Windows arms were not run.\n- The app's posting path was not run end to end. It already blocks on the warning.\n\nChangelog: grblHAL, Carvera and TinyG posts write no motion after refusing a first X/Y traverse with no stated clearance or retract plane (the `post` CLI no longer puts the refused move in the file)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1682\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
